[16.103174, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY ? Redis Unauth campaign\r\n====================================================\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER Analyst handoff Confidence: HIGH (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: redis-prod-01 Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.170\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered\r\nonly part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk\r\nfinding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\nT1133\r\nExternal Remote Services\r\n[persistence] step 1:\r\nunauthenticated Redis access (external service)\r\nT1059.004 Unix Shell\r\n[execution] step 2: shell execution\r\nvia CONFIG SET\r\nT1496\r\nResource Hijacking\r\n[impact] step 3: cryptomining\r\nT1053.003 Cron\r\n[execution] step 4: cron persistence\r\nT1574.006 Dynamic Linker Hijacking\r\n[stealth] step 5: LD_PRELOAD hijack\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\nip 198.51.100.170\r\nc2 update-redis[.]example[.]cn\r\npool stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]redis[.]evil[:]3333\r\nwallet 4A00000000000000000031c7d95fb9f3\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S.\r\nNational Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n\r\n\f"]
